{
  "note": "The harness census: one row per code file under tools/ (tools/test/ excluded, docs/tests.json is that folder's census) and scripts/, saying what each file is FOR. `role` is authored because no derivation supplies it; layer, lines, invocation, emits, named, and tested are stamped by tools/build/tools-index.mjs, whose --check mode runs in the lockstep suite. A blank role is a ledger entry, not a violation: it marks a file nobody has yet accounted for, the same discipline docs/tests.json applies to protects. Filed after the 2026-08-08 lib-kits migration showed what an unaccounted shelf costs; docs/code-layers.md names tools/ as the weak layer and this census is its accounting. (docs/tools.json is a different thing: the curated Tools gallery manifest.)",
  "layers": {
    "scripts": "standalone and portable: argv-driven, runs from any repo root, travels via the hub",
    "tools": "repo-root harness files that fit no folder below",
    "tools/build": "generators: snapshot a page or the lib into an offline artifact, or restamp a committed registry",
    "tools/concept-lab": "experimental ground, read-only prototypes that have not earned a place (its README states the admission rule)",
    "tools/render": "exercise a page headlessly: the jsdom logic render, the Chromium pixel render, and their shared CDN resolver",
    "tools/render/scenarios": "interaction drivers for npm run shot --script: each steers one page into one state before the pixels are taken"
  },
